It sounds like you have been hanging around that altar for a while
letting the monsters come to you, slaying them on the altar and then
sacrificing the corpses.  So far, so good.

-1 AC is not enough for level 10.  I presume you have gone through the
pile of stuff on the altar, trying on each piece of armor and keeping
the best?  Since it is on the altar you can avoid the cursed pieces.
Fortunately the samurai has intrinsic speed, so avoid getting encumbered
and you can usually escape from the monsters or keep your distance and
attack with projectiles.

Have you been to the Gnomish Mines yet?  If not I'd head back up and do
the mines.  You can strip some good armor off the corpses of all the
gnomes, dwarves etc. you will meet there.  If you happen to have
400 X experience level gold, offering it to the priest in the GM temple
could help with your AC problem.  Any priest will do; it doesn't have to
be a like-aligned priest.

It sounds like you are overdue for an identifying session.  Find some
way to engrave Elbereth (certain wands like fire and lightning will
engrave rather than writing in the dust), take off all armor (until you
ID Destroy Armor) and work through all those scrolls and potions.
Again, use the altar to ID blessed/uncursed/cursed status first.

: I am looking for a a polymorph wand as my first priority item but am I
: wrong? Suppose I get a wish from a potion or so. What should I do??

I wouldn't attach so much importance to polypiling.  That pile of stuff
won't go anywhere except for food items.  You can always head back to
level 5 when you find a wand.  In your shoes, my first wish would be +3
gray dragon scale mail (with magic resistance those polymorph traps
won't be a problem any more).

